{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-010", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Johnson Controls unveils industrial heat pump with 122 C output", "content": "<p>The Sabroe HitemHP uses butane or isobutane as its refrigerant and delivers between 100 kW and 1 MW of heating capacity. Johnson Controls says the single-stage system can operate at loads as low as 18% of its rated capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/johnson-controls-unveils-industrial-heat-pump-with-122-c-output/\">Johnson Controls unveils industrial heat pump with 122 C output</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/johnson-controls-unveils-industrial-heat-pump-with-122-c-output/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-011", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Google, esVolta pilot uses battery storage to ‘time-shift’ renewable energy credits", "content": "<p>LevelTen Energy, esVolta and Quintrace have piloted a way to bank surplus solar power in batteries and release it, together with hourly verified renewable credits, when Google’s electricity demand outstrips its clean-energy supply. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/google-esvolta-pilot-uses-battery-storage-to-time-shift-renewable-energy-credits/\">Google, esVolta pilot uses battery storage to ‘time-shift’ renewable energy credits</a> appeared first on <a href=\"ht", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/google-esvolta-pilot-uses-battery-storage-to-time-shift-renewable-energy-credits/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-012", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Inclusion by design: The leadership behaviours PV innovation needs", "content": "<p>Women in Solar+ Europe reflects this week on the leadership behaviours needed to strengthen innovation, psychological safety and collaboration across PV research and industry, following its workshop at EU PVSEC 2026 this week, co-organised with WIP Renewables. The discussion connected inclusion with how expertise shapes decisions. Its conclusions offer practical direction for PV teams and cross-sector partnerships.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/inclusion-by-d", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/inclusion-by-design-the-leadership-behaviours-pv-innovation-needs/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-013", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record", "[否定]loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Dry August pushes Dallas soiling losses towards 2% as North American GHI diverges", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, Solcast, a DNV company, reports that August irradiance fell across the Great Lakes but rose across the Pacific Northwest, south-central United States, and Mexico amid contrasting weather patterns.<br />\nDry conditions pushed Dallas soiling losses toward a record 2%, while Hurricane Lala brought extreme rain to Hawaii but left monthly irradiance only 4% below normal.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/dry-august-pushes", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/dry-august-pushes-dallas-soiling-losses-towards-2-as-north-american-ghi-diverges/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-014", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Chinese PV Industry Brief: CEEC launches 15 GW module procurement", "content": "<p>China Energy Engineering Corp. has launched a 15 GW module tender spanning TOPCon, HJT and BC technologies, while China South-to-North Water Diversion Group shortlisted bidders for 1.3 GW, with BC modules commanding an 8% premium over TOPCon.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/chinese-pv-industry-brief-ceec-launches-15-gw-module-procurement/\">Chinese PV Industry Brief: CEEC launches 15 GW module procurement</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.co", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/chinese-pv-industry-brief-ceec-launches-15-gw-module-procurement/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-015", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Very low cost rooftop solar slashes domestic energy cost – Part 3: African Countries", "content": "<p>There are 54 countries in the African Continent. Rooftop solar photovoltaics is growing rapidly in some African nations, but uptake is highly uneven across countries and is not measured comprehensively across all nations. It is clear that South Africa is far ahead of the rest of the continent (71% of all rooftop PV in Africa), while Nigeria, Kenya, Morocco and Egypt are emerging as important markets. Despite Africa’s abundant solar resources, a large gap persists between current rooftop solar", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/very-low-cost-rooftop-solar-slashes-domestic-energy-cost-part-3-african-countries/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-18-016", "date": "2026-09-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Italian inverter manufacturer Santerno set to resume production", "content": "<p>LEA Renergy has acquired Enertronica Santerno for €6 million and is now ready to restart inverter production. The group is targeting €40 million in revenue by 2030.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/italian-inverter-manufacturer-santerno-set-to-resume-production/\">Italian inverter manufacturer Santerno set to resume production</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/18/italian-inverter-manufacturer-santerno-set-to-resume-production/", "type": "rss"}]}
